        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "The $T _ { m }$and crystallization temperature (T ) values of the copolyesters were measured with a Seiko DSC 220C differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) instrument calibrated with pure indium as a standard (Japan). To eliminate the thermal history, samples (2.5 ± 0.5 mg) were heated to 280°C at a heating rate of 20°C/min and held there at 280°C for 1 min. T was measured while the samples were cooled to -50°C at a rate of 20°C/min, and during the third run, $T _ { m }$was measured at a heating rate of 20°C/min.",
        "table_locator": null
      },
